Hermes Agent attribution for memory_manager/edit.rs consolidation and exact-add intent
Source: https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent
Revision: 1fd18277267152893a8a24792b79213e7ca3f899

Adapted tools/memory_tool_store.py::MemoryStore.add/apply_batch/_batch:
validate the complete batch before a single committed mutation, pin exact reviewed
entries and skip exact duplicate adds. Anima ports these boundaries into a native
Rust memory manager and the host's existing single-snapshot MemoryMutation.
It uses exact source record IDs/content, canonical owner/scope/visibility and
explicit Write authority. Sources become historical Reflections with original
IDs/text/citations intact; one new summary Fact shares a discoverable group tag.
No fuzzy match, source deletion/citation retarget, user-profile target, file format,
Python runtime, private profile or credentials are imported. The group tag is
not immutable audit or proof that a model summary faithfully represents sources.
